0..63 Comment "// A row may name an instance of an interface by a label: `say`"
64..139 Comment "// performs `std.io.Console.Eff` through its instance `out`, apart from the"
140..214 Comment "// interface\'s default and from every other instance, so one row holds two"
215..283 Comment "// instances of one interface. The label is a parameter the function"
284..359 Comment "// abstracts, placed after every parameter it writes: a call supplies it by"
360..434 Comment "// name, `say[.out = c]()`, or omits it and passes the one instance of the"
435..510 Comment "// interface handled where the call stands, a capability scope\'s capability"
511..577 Comment "// or a label of the caller\'s own row (Brachthäuser, Schuster and"
578..649 Comment "// Ostermann, \"Effects as Capabilities: Effect Handlers and Lightweight"
650..707 Comment "// Effect Polymorphism\", OOPSLA 2020). What refuses is in"
708..762 Comment "// `../../pathological/control/named-instances.gandr`."
763..765 Comment "//"
766..781 Comment "// - see: #2271"
783..815 Comment "// The console\'s host interface."
